    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d421">

                <pb facs="0406" n="341" sameAs="frus:frus1936v03/pg341"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">865D.01/230: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Italy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Phillips</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Rome</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-12-24T13:00:00+01:00">December 24, 1936—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 24—9:35 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>550. My 548, December 24, 11 a.m.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d421-f1"/> In view of the
                    fact that 12 countries have already given <hi rendition="#italic">de facto</hi>
                    recognition to the new regime in Ethiopia, including all the great powers
                    particularly interested, can we not start the new year by some announcement to
                    the effect that the American Legation at Addis Ababa will shortly be transformed
                    into a consulate?</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Phillips</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
